
---
description: Use global agent-skills workflows
alwaysApply: true
---

# Agent skills routing

This project uses the global agent-skills install (not project-local copies):

- Skills: `~/.agents/skills/` → `/home/primozs/agent-skills/skills/`
- References: `~/.agents/references/` → `/home/primozs/agent-skills/references/`
- Personas (Cursor subagents): `~/.cursor/agents/` → `/home/primozs/agent-skills/agents/`

Before non-trivial technical work:

1. Route via the `using-agent-skills` skill.
2. Read and follow the matching skill under `~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.
3. Open linked checklists under `~/.agents/references/` when the skill points to them.
4. Prefer skills over guessing; the user does not need to say "read skill" each time.

## Personas (optional specialists)

Default to skills. Delegate to a persona via Task / subagent when the user wants a dedicated specialist pass (or clearly asks for review, security, test strategy, or web perf audit). Personas do not call other personas; you (or the user) orchestrate. Skills remain the *how* inside a persona when relevant.

| Persona | Prefer when |
|---------|-------------|
| `code-reviewer` | Full five-axis review before merge |
| `security-auditor` | Dedicated security / threat pass |
| `test-engineer` | Test strategy, coverage gaps, Prove-It |
| `web-performance-auditor` | Core Web Vitals / frontend perf audit |

Do not fan out personas on every small change.
